{%- comment -%}
  _includes/footer.liquid — PRD §4.7.2. FROZEN after Wave 0 (AGENTS.md §5).

  Hidden on Home — the guard lives in base.liquid (§4.7.2, §5.1). A footer is
  chrome, and §4.7.3's argument for keeping the toggle off "/" cannot hold while
  a footer sits under the envelope.

  Copy is theme-supplied (§4.5). rel="noreferrer" reinforces §7 Q3's
  Referrer-Policy at the element level: the header only applies on Netlify, and
  the secret this project protects IS the origin.

  The link is GUARDED on footerLinkUrl. Liquid renders a missing key as an empty
  string (§4.5), and href="" resolves to the CURRENT page — which would ship a
  focusable, unnamed link that navigates to itself. tests/copy.js (Wave 1a)
  should catch a missing key at build time; this guard is what keeps the failure
  from reaching a visitor if it ever doesn't.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign theme = themes[site.partyTheme] -%}
<footer class="site-footer">
  <p class="footer-line">
    {{ theme.footerLine }}
    {%- if theme.footerLinkUrl %}
    <a href="{{ theme.footerLinkUrl }}" rel="noreferrer">{{ theme.footerLinkText }}</a>
    {%- endif %}
  </p>
</footer>
